1
00:00:00,392 --> 00:00:02,062
(Leonard:)The thing is, someone's coming over.

2
00:00:02,227 --> 00:00:05,517
Well, no problem. I have three controllers.
The more the merrier.

3
00:00:05,898 --> 00:00:08,318
(Leonard:)Sheldon, it's a date.
I have a date coming over.

4
00:00:08,484 --> 00:00:09,694
(Sheldon:)Oh.

5
00:00:10,152 --> 00:00:13,402
(Sheldon:)Well, you can't blame me
for not jumping to that conclusion.

6
00:00:15,282 --> 00:00:17,912
Why? What's so unusual
about me having a date?

7
00:00:18,076 --> 00:00:20,706
- Well, statistically speaking...
- All right, all right.

8
00:00:20,871 --> 00:00:22,331
(Leonard:)Nevertheless, I have one now...

9
00:00:22,498 --> 00:00:25,918
...and I'd appreciate it if you would,
you know, make yourself scarce.

10
00:00:26,084 --> 00:00:28,874
(Sheldon:)I am a published theoretical physicist
with two doctorates...

11
00:00:29,046 --> 00:00:31,466
...and an IQ which can't be measured
by normal tests.

12
00:00:31,632 --> 00:00:33,922
(Sheldon:)How much scarcer could I be?

13
00:00:34,927 --> 00:00:38,307
(Leonard:)You know what I mean.
Could you just give us a little privacy?

14
00:00:38,472 --> 00:00:40,802
- You want me to leave the apartment?
- Yes.

15
00:00:40,974 --> 00:00:43,394
(Sheldon:)You mean just go someplace else
and be...

16
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,100
(Sheldon:)...someplace else?

17
00:00:45,562 --> 00:00:47,062
- Yes.
- But why should I leave?

18
00:00:47,231 --> 00:00:49,271
(Sheldon:)- This is my apartment too.
- I know it is.

19
00:00:49,441 --> 00:00:52,231
(Leonard:)If science ever discovers a second member
of your species...

20
00:00:52,402 --> 00:00:58,022
(Leonard:)...and you two would like some privacy,
I'd be happy to get out of your way.

